he required corpus.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Retirement Corpus = Annual Retirement Expenses ÷ Safe Withdrawal Rate\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Example: If your annual retirement expenses are ₹12,00,000 and you use a 4% safe withdrawal rate, the required retirement corpus is:\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 font-medium text-white\",\"children\":\"₹12,00,000 ÷ 0.04 = ₹3,00,00,000\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"FIRE Number Formula\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"FIRE Number = Annual Expenses × 25\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"The multiplier of 25 comes from the commonly referenced 4% withdrawal rule.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Example: If annual expenses are ₹12 lakh, your FIRE target is approximately:\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 font-medium text-white\",\"children\":\"₹12,00,000 × 25 = ₹3,00,00,000\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"edu-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"edu-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Retirement Planning Education\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",\"What Is Retirement Planning?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"What Is Retirement Planning?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Retirement planning is the process of estimating future expenses, choosing an appropriate investment strategy, and building enough wealth to support your lifestyle after regular employment ends.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"What Is a Retirement Corpus?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"What Is a Retirement Corpus?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A retirement corpus is the total amount of money you need invested so that you can withdraw from it during retirement without running out too early.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"What Is FIRE?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"What Is FIRE?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"FIRE means Financial Independence, Retire Early. The goal is to build enough invested wealth to cover expenses long before the traditional retirement age.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Understanding SWP\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Understanding SWP\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A Systematic Withdrawal Plan allows you to withdraw a fixed monthly amount from a portfolio. It is commonly used to turn accumulated wealth into retirement income.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"How Inflation Changes the Goal\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"How Inflation Changes the Goal\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"If today’s yearly expenses are ₹6 lakh and inflation is 6%, your retirement expense target many years later will be much higher. That is why inflation-adjusted retirement planning is essential.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Safe Withdrawal Rate Explained\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Safe Withdrawal Rate Explained\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A safe withdrawal rate estimates how much you can withdraw each year from your corpus while preserving the chance of long-term sustainability.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Sequence of Returns Risk\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Sequence of Returns Risk\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"If market returns are weak early in retirement, withdrawals can hurt your corpus more severely. This is why withdrawal planning must include a safety buffer.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Asset Allocation Strategy\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Asset Allocation Strategy\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Long accumulation phases often use more equity for growth, while retirement planning usually shifts toward a more balanced mix of equity and debt as risk tolerance changes.\"}]]}]]}],\"$L44\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"fire-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"fire-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"FIRE, Lean FIRE, Coast FIRE, and Fat FIRE\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"FIRE number explained\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Your FIRE number is often estimated as annual expenses multiplied by 25, which mirrors the 4% rule. It gives you a simple target for financial independence planning.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Lean FIRE vs Fat FIRE\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Lean FIRE targets a smaller, low-expense retirement lifestyle, while Fat FIRE targets a larger corpus that supports a more flexible and comfortable lifestyle.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Coast FIRE\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Coast FIRE means your invested corpus is already large enough to compound into retirement without new contributions, assuming the growth rate works as expected.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"compare-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"compare-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Retirement Calculator vs FIRE Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Retirement Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A retirement calculator focuses on estimating retirement corpus, future expenses, withdrawal rates, inflation impact, and retirement income needs based on a traditional retirement age.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"FIRE Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A FIRE calculator focuses on achieving financial independence as early as possible. It emphasizes savings rate, investment growth, and the FIRE number required to support expenses without active employment income.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"corpus-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"corpus-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"How Much Retirement Corpus Is Needed?\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"The retirement corpus required depends on your annual expenses, retirement age, life expectancy, inflation rate, expected investment returns, and safe withdrawal rate. A common retirement planning calculator estimate uses annual expenses multiplied by 25, which corresponds to the widely known 4% withdrawal rule.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"For example, if your annual retirement expenses are ₹12 lakh, a retirement corpus of approximately ₹3 crore may be required. Investors seeking additional safety often target 30× to 33× annual expenses to account for inflation, healthcare costs, and sequence of returns risk.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A retirement planning calculator helps estimate this corpus more accurately by considering future inflation-adjusted expenses, expected portfolio returns, retirement duration, and withdrawal strategy.\"}]]}]]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"expense-corpus-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"expense-corpus-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Retirement Corpus Required for Different Monthly Expenses\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"w-full text-left text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"className\":\"border-b border-white/10\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"Monthly Expense\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"Annual Expense\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"Corpus at 4% Withdrawal Rate\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"border-b border-white/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹25,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹3 lakh\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹75 lakh\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"border-b border-white/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹50,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹6 lakh\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹1.5 crore\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"border-b border-white/5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹1,00,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹12 lakh\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹3 crore\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹2,00,000\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹24 lakh\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"p-4\",\"children\":\"₹6 crore\"}]]}]]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"A common retirement planning guideline estimates corpus requirements using a 4% safe withdrawal rate. Under this approach, the retirement corpus is approximately 25 times annual expenses. Investors seeking additional safety may target a larger corpus to account for inflation, healthcare costs, taxes, and market uncertainty.\"}]]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"age-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"age-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Retirement Planning by Age\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Retirement Planning in Your 20s and 30s\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Investors in their 20s and 30s usually have the advantage of time. Long investment horizons allow compounding to work more effectively, making SIP investing and equity-oriented portfolios popular choices for retirement wealth creation.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Retirement Planning in Your 40s and 50s\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"As retirement approaches, investors often focus on increasing savings, reducing debt, reviewing asset allocation, and building a realistic retirement corpus target. Portfolio preservation gradually becomes more important alongside growth.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"factors-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"factors-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Factors That Affect Retirement Corpus\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",\"Inflation\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Inflation\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Higher inflation increases future living costs and requires a larger retirement corpus.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Healthcare Costs\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Healthcare Costs\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Medical expenses often rise faster than general inflation and should be included in retirement planning.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Life Expectancy\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Life Expectancy\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Longer retirement periods require a larger corpus and a more sustainable withdrawal strategy.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Investment Returns\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Investment Returns\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Expected portfolio growth influences how much capital is needed before retirement.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Withdrawal Rate\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Withdrawal Rate\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Lower withdrawal rates generally improve sustainability but require a larger corpus.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"Lifestyle Choices\",{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Lifestyle Choices\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Travel, housing, family support, and discretionary spending can significantly affect retirement needs.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"mistakes-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"mistakes-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Common Retirement Mistakes\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Mistakes to avoid\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"Starting too late and assuming compounding will somehow make up the gap.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Starting too late and assuming compounding will somehow make up the gap.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Ignoring inflation and using today’s expenses as if they will never rise.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Ignoring inflation and using today’s expenses as if they will never rise.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Using a withdrawal rate that is too aggressive for the portfolio.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Using a withdrawal rate that is too aggressive for the portfolio.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Forgetting healthcare, family obligations, and emergency costs.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Forgetting healthcare, family obligations, and emergency costs.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Relying on one asset class without rebalancing.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Relying on one asset class without rebalancing.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Assuming the same return rate year after year without a margin of safety.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Assuming the same return rate year after year without a margin of safety.\"]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Better strategies\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 space-y-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"Use equity-heavy allocation during accumulation for long-term growth.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Use equity-heavy allocation during accumulation for long-term growth.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Shift toward balanced allocation as retirement approaches.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Shift toward balanced allocation as retirement approaches.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Keep a debt or cash buffer for near-term withdrawals.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Keep a debt or cash buffer for near-term withdrawals.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Review inflation assumptions every year.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Review inflation assumptions every year.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Recalculate your corpus after major life changes.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Recalculate your corpus after major life changes.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Test conservative and base-case scenarios before depending on a target.\",{\"children\":[\"• \",\"Test conservative and base-case scenarios before depending on a target.\"]}]]}]]}]]}]]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"allocation-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"allocation-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Asset Allocation and Sequence Risk\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Best asset allocation strategies\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Equity-heavy allocation is often used during the accumulation phase because it offers higher long-term growth potential. Near retirement, many investors shift to a more balanced mix of equity and debt for stability and withdrawal planning.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Sequence of returns risk\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Sequence of returns risk matters because poor early returns combined with withdrawals can reduce portfolio longevity faster than the same returns arriving later in retirement. This is one reason retirement planning should include a buffer.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"india-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"india-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"Retirement Planning in India\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"How much money is needed to retire in India?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"The answer depends on city, household size, lifestyle, healthcare costs, and the level of inflation you expect over time. A retirement corpus calculator helps personalize the number instead of relying on a generic estimate.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Inflation impact in India\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Inflation can significantly increase the cost of retirement, especially when planning across long horizons. That is why inflation-adjusted retirement calculations are more useful than static expense assumptions.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-labelledby\":\"people-search-heading\",\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"people-search-heading\",\"className\":\"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"People Also Search For\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"FIRE Number Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Calculate the portfolio size required to achieve financial independence using annual expenses and withdrawal rates.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold\",\"children\":\"SWP Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-xs leading-6 text-white/65\",\"children\":\"Estimate monthly retirement income and portfolio sustainability through systematic withdrawals.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,